Barca hoped to overwhelm ownership yet were feeble to control Real&#8217;s counterattacks and went behind when Federico Valverde leaped a Jordi Alba tackle to carry down the pitch, taking care of Lucas Vazquez whose low cross was turned in by Benzema&#8217;s glorious backheel.

Genuine got Barca out on the break again when Vinicius Jr. hustled on to a Luka Modric pass and was felled by Ronald Araujo. The free kick was in ideal reach for Kroos, whose shot ricocheted off the rear of Sergino Dest to wrong-foot Barca manager Marc-Andre ter Stegen.

Genuine were inches from scoring a third when Valverde again destroyed Barca&#8217;s left-hand side and smacked the far post, Vazquez jumping on the bounce back yet taking shots directly at Ter Stegen.

Barca scarcely raised Real any ruckus until the finish of the principal half, when Lionel Messi hit the far post directly from a corner. The Argentine had a superior possibility minutes after the fact from inside the space yet couldn&#8217;t beat Madrid&#8217;s Thibaut Courtois.

